{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310643,"nonce":"qUgVdhh1B/C8YNCg28suTdGytjU=","title":"Holding an inkwell FunctionValue across run_passes segfaults, because global DCE erases unreferenced declarations","message":"`module.run_passes(\"default\u003cO3\u003e\", ...)` includes global DCE, which **erases**\ndeclarations nothing referenced. Every `FunctionValue`/`GlobalValue` held across\nthat call then points at freed LLVM memory, and the next `count_basic_blocks()`\non one is a SIGSEGV inside `LLVMCountBasicBlocks` — in LLVM's own library, with\na backtrace that names your function but no bad line in it.\n\n**Rule: names survive the optimiser, values do not.** Capture\n`llvm_fn.get_name().to_string_lossy().to_string()` before running passes and\nre-resolve with `self.module.get_function(\u0026name)` afterwards. A name that no\nlonger resolves is a declaration nothing referenced — which by definition needs\nno address bound to it, so skipping it is correct rather than a fallback.\n\nThe whole-module path in `llvm_jit_backend.rs` already encodes this and says so:\n\n```rust\n// Get function symbols before finalize (we need names for global storage)\nlet function_symbols = backend.get_function_symbols();\nbackend.finalize()?;          // \u003c- runs the passes\n```\n\nThis is the same family as [[bugs_irfunctionid_is_module_local]] and\n[[bugs_internedstring_display_forged_names]]: an identity that is only valid\ninside one scope, used outside it.\n\nFound via `gdb -batch -ex run -ex \"bt 25\" --args \u003cexe\u003e \u003cargs\u003e` on the NUC after\nthe tiered path segfaulted; the tier-event log showed `llvm_queue_start` with no\nmatching `llvm_queue_finish` and no `llvm_queue_error`, which localises a fault\nto *inside* compilation rather than inside compiled code.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_llvm_values_dangle_across_the_optimiser` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}